  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the second of six runs: 8 witnesses, 12 names, no compositions, and one narrowing that I declared.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **`VACUOUS`.** The check that no other road edge on the same highway is nearer (`st_on_way e2 h`) never changed a verdict, because every edge in my scenes lay on that highway. I added `branch_4` (compliant): the nearest edge belongs to a parallel road, and the car's wheels point toward its own highway's farther edge.\n2. **`OK`.**\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_533.lean`)\n- **Class:** the vehicle aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **Applicability:** the vehicle is halted, has nobody in it, and sits on some highway whose grade exceeds `p.grade_resolution` in magnitude.\n- **Obligation:** the engine is off and the parking brake is set. Also, for every such highway, the steering angle exceeds `p.steer_angle_resolution` toward the side of the nearest road edge on that highway (left-positive, matched to the sign of that edge's lateral offset).\n\n**Choices the node left open**\n- **Which highway:** the wheel duty applies to every highway the applicability picks out. Engine and brake don't depend on the highway, so they're checked once, outside that loop.\n- **Equally near edges on both sides:** turning the wheels toward either one complies. I declared this as a narrowing on s5.\n- **Zero-offset edge** (the car's reference point lies inside the edge region): it gives no side, so no wheel position complies. This follows from the record's sign rule, so I noted it in the header rather than declaring it.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_533.lean`)\n- The six planned ones: forbid, permit, idle, blind (parking brake masked), branch_1 (wheels straight), branch_2 (driver inside).\n- Two I added:\n  - `branch_3`: nearest curb on the left, wheels turned left; compliant.\n  - `branch_4`: as above; compliant.\n\nThe full run log is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
